{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"defc6eefe08ffd03dc51facb93a6612aafea8c7fa5d34425c1f3a77e3ad1f07e","slug":"future.fairmappings","location":"/future/FAIRMappings.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Reusable Mappings as FAIR Resources","content_includes_title":false,"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","free":true,"CC":true}},"github":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook","copyright":"We appreciate constructive feedback. Contact us at\n[cdif-feedback@codata.org](mailto:cdif-feedback@codata.org) or file a GitHub Issue at\n[Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/issues/new/choose](https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/issues/new/choose).\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 Committee on Data of the International Science Council (CODATA). The Cross Domain Interoperability Framework (CDIF) is licenced under CC-BY-4.0.\n","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/blob/main/future/FAIRMappings.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/edit/main/future/FAIRMappings.md","thumbnail":"/cdifbook/preview-2026-05/build/74a4144c2e90e9bc69f56de8f0675705.jpeg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"FAIRMappings.md","url":"/cdifbook/preview-2026-05/build/FAIRMappings-a8302801ef30058c0f899ad8020a0287.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is recognized that transformations to both data and metadata at several levels are a critical part of data integration. The mappings used to inform transformations are a critical aspect of this, being both needed provenance information and also potentially providing a reusable FAIR resource in their own right. There is an RDA group working on ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"GcWtysy6pf"},{"type":"link","url":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/rda-fair-mappings/use-cases/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"FAIR Mappings","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"kzygUAs59n"}],"urlSource":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/rda-fair-mappings/use-cases/","key":"b1CvuKfVxA"},{"type":"text","value":", and the CDIF WG follows this work and attempts to align with it. Currently, the use of A Simple Standard for Sharing Ontology mappings (","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"f2h8rPYkay"},{"type":"link","url":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/sssom/dev/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSSOM","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"b6KjFxLaga"}],"urlSource":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/sssom/dev/","key":"lWkm68BZgU"},{"type":"text","value":") is seen as a useful standard for the expression of mappings, with the RDF Mapping Language ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"chETyqbUmK"},{"type":"link","url":"https://rml.io/specs/rml/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"RML","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"UVGIkWSzzb"}],"urlSource":"https://rml.io/specs/rml/","key":"UZy0f2XGdi"},{"type":"text","value":" also proving to be of interest, This is an area where more work remains to be done, but will be the subject of a CDIF profile in the not-too-distant future.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"E3s5THFXl1"}],"key":"D6jUsp6IqI"},{"type":"comment","value":" cdif-foote